course: dictionary
lesson: 1367
title: Canopy: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Canopy is a noun with three main meanings: the top layer of leaves in a forest, a cover held up over something, and the clear cover over a plane's cockpit.
explain: «The canopy is the thick roof of leaves and branches high in a rainforest.» The words rainforest, leaves and branches are the clues. They tell you canopy means the forest's top layer, not a cloth over a bed.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The bed had a canopy of pale blue cloth.» Try "roof of leaves" here and it sounds wrong, so this canopy is a cover held up over something.
fact: A canopy is the top layer of leaves and branches in a forest, like a roof.
fact: A canopy can also be a cloth or roof held up over something, like a bed, a stall or a doorway.
fact: «High above the Amazon floor the tree tops join into a green roof called the canopy.»
fact: Most animals in a rainforest live in the canopy, which is full of sunlight, fruit and flowers.
fact: Canopy can also mean the clear cover over a plane's cockpit, or the cloth of a parachute.
exercise: «The canopy is the thick roof of leaves and branches high in a rainforest.» What does canopy mean here? | A cloth held up over a bed | *The top layer of leaves and branches in a forest | A clear cover over a cockpit | A stall at a market
exercise: Mia's pram had a canopy to keep off the rain. What does canopy mean here? | A harmless mist | The clear cover of a plane | A tall green tree | *A cover held up over something
exercise: What is the best clue for the meaning of canopy in «High above the Amazon floor the tree tops join into a green roof called the canopy.»? | High above the Amazon | called | *tree tops join into a green roof | Amazon
test: The rain bounced off the canopy over the market stall. What does canopy mean here? | A tall tree | The clear cover of a cockpit | *A cover held up over something | The top layer of a rainforest
test: The pilot pulled back the canopy and climbed out of the plane. What does canopy mean here? | *The clear cover over a plane's cockpit | A cloth of a bed | The top of a forest | A roof of leaves
exam: «When researchers sprayed a harmless mist into single canopy trees, beetles of hundreds of kinds fell out.» Which meaning of canopy fits best here? | *The top layer of leaves and branches in the forest | A parachute's cloth | A cover over a plane's cockpit | A cloth held up over a bed
